21 CFR 820.35 adds the following to the record control requirements of the incorporated standard:

- The name of the device (820.35(a)(1));
- The date the complaint was received (820.35(a)(2));
- A unique device identifier (UDI) or universal product code (UPC), and any other device identification (820.35(a)(3));
- The name, address and phone number of the complainant (820.35(a)(4));
- The nature and details of the complaint (820.35(a)(5));
- Any correction or corrective action taken (820.35(a)(6));
- Any reply to the complainant (820.35(a)(7));
- The name of the device serviced (820.35(b)(1));
- Any UDI or UPC, and any other device identification (820.35(b)(2));
- The date of service (820.35(b)(3));
- The individual(s) who serviced the device (820.35(b)(4));
- The service performed (820.35(b)(5));
- Any test and inspection data (820.35(b)(6));

The record control requirements incorporated by reference are 820.7 and 820.35(a), and the servicing activities requirement is 820.35(b).

